Package: uzunyx-editions
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: emi <285864120+antarest47@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: uzunyx-lookandfeel (>= 0.18.0), uzunyx-wallpapers (>= 0.7.0), uzunyx-colors (>= 0.2.0), plasma-workspace (>= 4:6.7), systemsettings, libkf6config-bin, python3, python3-gi, pkexec, libkf6kcmutilsquick6, libkf6i18n6, libkf6configcore6, libkf6coreaddons6, libqt6qml6, libqt6core6t64
Recommends: tsunyx-launcher, uzunyx-plymouth, uzunyx-keys
Description: switch between the Uzunyx editions (Akane and Sora)
 A System Settings module, "Uzunyx Edition" (Colors & Themes), with a card
 for each edition. Applying one changes, without touching the panels or the
 icons, its global theme (colors, window decoration…), desktop wallpaper,
 lock screen wallpaper and the logo on the panel's launcher button, and,
 if asked, the login screen (SDDM) background and the boot splash
 (Plymouth, from uzunyx-plymouth) for all users.
 .
 Plasma only applies a global theme's wallpaper together with its desktop
 layout, which replaces the panels; this does it on its own.
 .
 The work is done by the uzunyx-edition command (also usable from a
 terminal: "uzunyx-edition set sora"). The login and boot screen parts
 run a small helper as root through pkexec.
